goal goal.semctx.honest-project-evidence
  statement: Project policy explicitly selects repository-relative candidates across the monorepo while keeping selection, capability, freshness and behavioral proof distinct.
  status: declared
  provenance: author
  appliesAtLevel: 5
  file: docs/reference/configuration.md
  tag: project-evidence

invariant invariant.semctx.project-evidence-honesty
  statement: Keep invariant, critical-contract and security rules strict; never treat an analyzed file, a fresh index or a policy PASS as proof of complete coverage or passing runtime behavior.
  status: declared
  provenance: author
  appliesAtLevel: 4
  serves: goal.semctx.honest-project-evidence
  file: docs/adr/0010-multilanguage-plane-a-capability-and-authority.md
  tag: project-evidence

unknown unknown.semctx.project-negative-completeness
  statement: Index health reports AMBIGUOUS_LAYOUT for the semctx identities at apps/cli and plugins/claude-code, plus NEGATIVE_COMPLETENESS_MISSING; negative completeness remains unproven.
  status: declared
  provenance: author
  appliesAtLevel: 4
  tag: coverage

unknown unknown.semctx.project-analysis-boundaries
  statement: JavaScript hooks and site code, JSON/YAML configuration and shell scripts have no registered analyzer here; Python lacks inferred calls, test coverage and negative completeness, while Markdown and the example SQL migration receive structural classification only.
  status: declared
  provenance: author
  appliesAtLevel: 4
  file: docs/reference/configuration.md
  tag: coverage

